            <ArticleTitle>Multi-energy spectral CT: adding value in emergency body imaging.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10140-017-1569-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most vendors offer scanners capable of dual- or multi-energy computed tomography (CT) imaging. Advantages of multi-energy CT scanning include superior tissue characterization, detection of subtle iodine uptake differences, and opportunities to reduce contrast dose. However, utilization of this technology in the emergency department (ED) remains low. The purpose of this pictorial essay is to illustrate the value of multi-energy CT scanning in emergency body imaging.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
